.SH "NAME"
pcre2_code_free \- free a compiled pattern
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBvoid\fP pcre2_code_free(\fBpcre2_code\fP *\fIcode\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
If \fIcode\fP is \f(CRNULL\fP, this function does nothing. Otherwise, \fIcode\fP must
point to a compiled pattern. This function frees its memory, including any
memory used by the JIT compiler. If the compiled pattern was created by a call
to pcre2_code_copy_with_tables(), the memory for the character tables is
also freed.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.